            <ArticleTitle>The long-term outcome of facial pain treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The long-term outcome of facial pain treatment is largely unknown. This study reports the results of a 4-yr review which indicated that conservative treatments including drug therapy and counselling are effective for 70% of patients. Refractory pain was associated with a long complex history of pain, a preoccupation with physical symptoms and poor psychosocial adjustment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
